{
  "dom_id": "step-q61174",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "A concrete mix weighs $600$ kilograms. Of this amount, $19.5%$ represents the weight of the crushed stone in the mix. How much crushed stone is there in the concrete mix?",
  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the weight of the concrete mix, which is $600$ kilograms. The percentage is $19.5%,$ and the part is the weight of the crushed stone in the mix.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n19.5%=19.5÷100=0.195\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =19.5%\\times 600 \\\\  & =0.195\\times 600 \\\\  & =117\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $19.5%$ of $600$ is $117.$ Thus, there are $117$ kilograms of crushed stone in the concrete mix.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n19.5%=\\frac{19.5}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =19.5%\\times 600 \\\\  & =\\frac{19.5}{100}\\times 600 \\\\  & =19.5\\times \\frac{600}{100} \\\\  & =19.5\\times 6 \\\\  & =117\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $19.5%$ of $600$ is $117.$ Thus, there are $117$ kilograms of crushed stone in the concrete mix.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
